THOUGHT: I will output a single bash command that sequentially displays the plan file, prints the JSON spec, and shows any previous train feedback. This uses simple `cat` and `python3 -c` invocations to avoid heredoc quoting issues.

<mswea_bash_command>
cat "$PLAN_PATH" && \
python3 -c "import json,os; spec=json.load(open(os.environ['PLAN_JSON_PATH'])); print(json.dumps(spec,indent=2))" && \
python3 -c "import os,json; tp=os.getenv('TRAIN_COMPARE_PATH',''); 
if not tp: 
    print('No train feedback (first attempt).') 
else: 
    data=json.load(open(tp)); 
    print('=== PREVIOUS ATTEMPT TRAIN COMPARISON ==='); 
    print(f'net_change: {data[\"net_change\"]:+d}'); 
    print(f'improvements: {data[\"improvement_count\"]}'); 
    print(f'regressions: {data[\"regression_count\"]}'); 
    print('regressed_ids:', data.get('regressed_ids',[])); 
    print('improved_ids:', data.get('improved_ids',[]))"
</mswea_bash_command>

